  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If there were such a thing as a “superfood,” cruciferous vegetables like broccoli would certainly be wearing the cape. Along with kale, collards, cabbage, bok choy, cauliflower, and many others in that vegetable family, crucifers contain a relatively unique class of phytonutrients that can potentially help prevent DNA damage, metastatic cancer spread, and lymphoma; activate defenses against pathogens and pollutants; boost your liver detox enzymes; target breast cancer stem cells; and reduce the risk of prostate cancer progression. That’s why I include cruciferous veggies in my Daily Dozen healthiest-of-healthy-foods checklist. For more information and all of my videos on broccoli, </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/broccoli/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">check out the topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Recipe: Mexican-Inspired Bowl</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/mexican-inspired-bowl/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-89732\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"198\" height=\"198\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-1536x1536.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-2048x2048.jpg 2048w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/mexican-inspired-bowl-5-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 198px) 100vw, 198px\"/></a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you’ve found yourself with a sudden hankering for broccoli, try this recipe from Ángela, our Spanish Social Media and Program Coordinator. With broccoli, beans, whole grains, and a homemade salsa, her recipe will check off several of your Daily Dozen boxes for the day. </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/mexican-inspired-bowl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Get the free recipe here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and watch a video on how it’s made on </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CT5HMaVpYZq/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">our Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4><b>Host a Screening</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-89730 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/host-a-screening.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Share the latest in evidence-based nutrition with your community by hosting a free screening of my “</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Die</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">” or “</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evidence-Based Weight Loss</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">” presentation. Each video runs for approximately one hour. Your free Digital Event Kit will include </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">the video, an introduction to NutritionFacts, a fun trivia game for attendees, and tips for hosting</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. For more information and to sign up, </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/screenings/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">go here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Volunteer Spotlight:</b> <b>Midge Constantino</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-89736\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-1024x1363.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"198\" height=\"264\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-1024x1363.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-960x1278.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-768x1022.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-1154x1536.jpg 1154w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-1539x2048.jpg 1539w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-1200x1597.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-720x958.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-540x719.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/volunteer-photo-scaled.jpg 1923w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 198px) 100vw, 198px\"/></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I’ve been a volunteer for NutritionFacts for a couple of years. I assist on a variety of projects, but my primary role is to compile lists of videos that are added as YouTube cards accompanying the recordings of Dr. Greger’s Live Q&amp;As. His mission of sharing evidence-based nutrition information to the general public is incredibly important, since misinformation sadly abounds. It’s been such an honor to help support NutritionFacts in my own little way.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I believe that breakfast is the most important meal of the day, and my favorite is Chocolate Oatmeal from </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-die-cookbook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The How Not to Die Cookbook</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. It’s yummy, very easy to prepare, and sustains me throughout the morning.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Top Three Videos</b></h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88270\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"X-ray image of human standing\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-07-do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-vegans-have-lower-bone-mineral-density-and-higher-risk-of-osteoporosis/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Do Vegans Have Lower Bone Mineral Density and Higher Risk of Osteoporosis?</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Those eating plant-based tend to be so much slimmer that their bone mass may suffer.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88147\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Assortment of vegetables, dried beans, and berries\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-03-the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-healthy-aging/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Best Diet for Healthy Aging</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Swapping just 1 percent of plant protein in place of animal protein was associated with signiﬁcantly less age-related deﬁcit accumulation.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88262\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Test dish in hand of scientist\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/59-06-antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/antibiotic-resistance-genes-in-the-guts-of-vegetarians-vs-meat-eaters/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Antibiotic Resistance Genes in the Guts of Vegetarians vs. Meat-Eaters</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Those eating plant-based have a reduced load of antibiotic resistance genes in their gut.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><em>P.S. We hit 200 million lifetime YouTube views! <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As you know, I made it my life’s work to reach as many people as possible with health information that can change and save lives. I’m grateful to all of you for watching and sharing these videos, helping to spread the healthy-living message.</span></em></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Live Q&amp;A TODAY </b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-68737 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"image of dr greger\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every month, I do a live Q&amp;A right from my treadmill, and the next one is today, October 20!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At 3 pm ET, tune in on our </span><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Facebook</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> page, </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">YouTube</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> channel, or (new!) directly on </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NutritionFacts.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can find links to past live Q&amp;As </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on NutritionFacts.org. If that’s not enough, remember, I have an </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">audio podcast</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to keep you company, too. </span></p>"
